# `-d ovh` only — the OVH prod-like test box. Read as [.kamal/secrets-common, .kamal/secrets.ovh];
# .kamal/secrets (base) is NOT read. Safe for git: references and commands only, never a raw
# credential.
#
# CHUNK_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY AND CHUNK_ACCESS_KEY_ID WERE HERE — the Cloudflare R2 token and access
# key id for bucket maker-chunks-prod, from when the maker app resolved a chunk store of its own.
# Arc D Part 2 handed the chunk store to the `sync` accessory (chaim354/tinkerex-sync, its own
# env), and nothing in this repo has read STORAGE_BACKEND or any CHUNK_* storage knob since
# (§7, §14a) — so both were dead. Dead in a secrets file is NOT free: Kamal's
# InlineCommandSubstitution runs every `$(…)` in a parsed file EAGERLY rather than lazily per key,
# so each one was a 1Password read on every `-d ovh` deploy for a value no container consumed.
# Removed from config/deploy.ovh.yml's env.secret in the same change. The 1Password items are
# untouched (op://tinkerex/R2/…), so an s3-backed OVH library can still resolve them if that is
# the backend this destination eventually declares.
#
# ⚠️ THOSE TWO NAMES WERE SHARED WITH THE UNRAID LEGS WHILE THE CREDENTIALS WERE NOT — R2 here,
# SeaweedFS in .kamal/secrets — which is why they could never have lived in secrets-common. That
# rule still binds for anything added below (docs/invariants/deploy-secrets.md, §14g).

# SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN — this destination's own app never SENDS it. It declares no LIBRARY_BACKEND, so
# it inherits chunk_remote and cannot boot it at all; see config/deploy.ovh.yml's CHUNK_REMOTE_URL
# comment for that open decision. Required here anyway, and structurally rather than by choice:
# the `sync` accessory (config/deploy.yml, Arc D Task 2) declares SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN as ITS OWN
# secret, and `accessories:` is never overridden by a destination overlay — so it folds into EVERY
# destination's merged config, this one included. Verified against Kamal::Configuration.raw_config,
# not assumed; test/deploy_hygiene_test.rb re-derives it on every run. NOT in secrets-common, on
# explicit instruction (§14g; unlike SECRET_KEY_BASE, which is — see that file's own comment).
# The fullest version of this argument lives with the accessory itself, in config/deploy.yml.
SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN=$(bin/secret SYNC_ADMIN_TOKEN 'op://tinkerex/tinkerex-sync-admin-token/password')
